  (4, $p$Security of Personal Information$p$, $p$AUDIT LOGGING & MONITORING$p$, 16, $p$Are audit logs reviewed regularly for anomalous or suspicious activity, with automated alerting configured for high-risk events (bulk downloads, privilege escalation, off-hours access)?$p$, $p$$p$, $p$POPIA s.19 | ISO 27002 cl.8.16 (Monitoring activities)$p$, $p$High$p$, $p$SIEM use case/alert rule documentation; alert log with investigation records; security operations weekly review reports; evidence of escalation and resolution of flagged events$p$, $p$Configure SIEM alerting for high-risk events: bulk data downloads, off-hours access, privilege escalation, repeated failed authentications, access to sensitive data categories. Assign a security operations analyst to review alerts daily. Document and investigate all triggered alerts.$p$, $p$large$p$, $p$popia.s4.q16$p$),
