  (4, $p$Security of Personal Information$p$, $p$BACKUP, RECOVERY & BUSINESS CONTINUITY$p$, 21, $p$Are backup media and backup storage environments subject to the same access controls, encryption, and security monitoring as primary systems processing personal information?$p$, $p$$p$, $p$POPIA s.19 | ISO 27002 cl.8.13, cl.8.24 (Use of cryptography); ISO 27701 cl.6.10$p$, $p$Critical$p$, $p$Backup storage access control configuration (role-based access, MFA for backup console); backup media encryption evidence; backup environment audit logs; network segmentation diagrams showing backup network isolation$p$, $p$Apply the same access control standards (RBAC, MFA, least privilege) to backup systems and storage as to production systems. Encrypt all backup data at rest and in transit. Segment the backup network. Include backup systems in vulnerability scanning and security monitoring scope.$p$, $p$large$p$, $p$popia.s4.q21$p$),
