  (4, $p$Security of Personal Information$p$, $p$BACKUP, RECOVERY & BUSINESS CONTINUITY$p$, 23, $p$Is backup media (physical tapes, drives, cloud snapshots) subject to a documented lifecycle management process including secure labelling, tracking, transport controls, and secure disposal at end-of-life?$p$, $p$$p$, $p$POPIA s.19 | ISO 27002 cl.7.10 (Storage media), cl.7.14 (Secure disposal or re-use of equipment)$p$, $p$High$p$, $p$Backup media inventory and tracking register; tape/drive labelling and classification records; media transport procedure (sealed courier, chain of custody); secure disposal certificates for decommissioned media (DoD 5220.22-M or equivalent)$p$, $p$Implement a media lifecycle management procedure covering: labelling, inventory tracking, encrypted transport (if physical), and secure disposal. Use a certified data destruction provider for physical media and obtain destruction certificates. Retain certificates for a minimum of 3 years.$p$, $p$large$p$, $p$popia.s4.q23$p$),
