  (4, $p$Security of Personal Information$p$, $p$THIRD-PARTY & SUPPLIER SECURITY$p$, 26, $p$Are third-party operator and supplier security controls reviewed or assessed at least annually, including review of audit reports, penetration test results, or re-assessment questionnaires?$p$, $p$$p$, $p$POPIA s.21 | ISO 27002 cl.5.19 (Information security in supplier relationships), cl.5.22 (Monitoring, review and change management of supplier services)$p$, $p$High$p$, $p$Annual supplier review records; updated security questionnaires or audit reports (ISO 27001, SOC 2); supplier risk re-assessment documentation; corrective action tracking for supplier deficiencies$p$, $p$Implement an annual supplier security review process for all operators processing personal information. Obtain updated security assurance (questionnaire or independent audit report). Escalate and track remediation of identified deficiencies. Terminate or limit processing by suppliers who cannot demonstrate adequate controls.$p$, $p$large$p$, $p$popia.s4.q26$p$),
