[NIST SP 800-171]  3.8.3 (Sanitise or destroy system components containing CUI before disposal); 3.8.4 (Mark media with necessary CUI markings)$p$, $p$Critical$p$, $p$Disposal and de-identification procedure; system-level deletion configuration (secure delete, crypto-shredding for encrypted data); disposal log with data category, volume, method, responsible party; destruction certificates for physical media; de-identification methodology documentation$p$, $p$Implement a formal disposal procedure for personal information. For digital data, use cryptographic erasure (if encrypted) or certified secure deletion tools. For physical media, engage a certified destruction provider and obtain certificates. Maintain a disposal log. For de-identification, document the method and test that re-identification is not feasible.$p$, $p$all$p$, $p$popia.s4.q28$p$),
  (4, $p$Security of Personal Information$p$, $p$DATA RETENTION, ARCHIVING & SECURE DISPOSAL$p$, 29, $p$Are disposal and de-identification events captured in a Disposal Register, reviewed by the IO, and reported on at least annually?$p$, $p$$p$, $p$POPIA s.14 | ISO 27701 cl.7.4.8; ISO 27002 cl.8.10$p$, $p$Medium$p$, $p$Disposal Register (date, PI category, data volume/count, disposal method, performed by, IO review signature); annual disposal report to management; integration with ROPA update process$p$, $p$Maintain a centralised Disposal Register. Require IO review and sign-off for all disposal events involving special categories of personal information or bulk PI disposal. Report disposal metrics (volumes, categories, methods) to management annually. Integrate disposal completion records with the ROPA to keep processing activities current.$p$, $p$large$p$, $p$popia.s4.q29$p$),
  (4, $p$Security of Personal Information$p$, $p$SECURITY AWARENESS & TRAINING$p$, 30, $p$Does the organisation conduct mandatory security and privacy awareness training for all staff with access to personal information at onboarding and at least annually thereafter, with completion records maintained?$p$, $p$$p$, $p$[POPIA]  s.19 (Security safeguards); s.55 (IO duties include encouraging compliance)
