[NIST SP 800-171]  3.2.1 (Ensure personnel are aware of security risks); 3.2.2 (Ensure personnel are trained to carry out responsibilities)$p$, $p$Critical$p$, $p$Training programme content (covering POPIA obligations, data handling, phishing, incident reporting, clean desk, password hygiene); training completion records by staff member and date; annual retraining schedule; new joiner onboarding training evidence$p$, $p$Implement a mandatory annual security and privacy awareness training programme. Ensure training covers: POPIA employee obligations, phishing recognition, incident reporting, acceptable use, clean desk, password hygiene, and DSAR procedures. Record completion for every staff member. Integrate with onboarding. Report completion rates to management quarterly.$p$, $p$all$p$, $p$popia.s4.q30$p$),
  (4, $p$Security of Personal Information$p$, $p$SECURITY AWARENESS & TRAINING$p$, 31, $p$Are staff who handle special categories of personal information (health data, biometric data, financial data) provided with role-specific, enhanced privacy and security training?$p$, $p$$p$, $p$POPIA s.26 (Special PI conditions) | ISO 27701 cl.6.4; ISO 27002 cl.6.3$p$, $p$High$p$, $p$Role-specific training content for special category PI handlers; training attendance records; assessment scores or completion confirmations; training needs analysis documenting roles in scope$p$, $p$Identify all roles that process special categories of personal information (s.26 of POPIA). Develop and deliver role-specific training covering the heightened obligations, consent requirements, and security controls applicable to special PI. Conduct annually and when roles or processing activities change.$p$, $p$large$p$, $p$popia.s4.q31$p$),
